{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:30:51Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 16, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Spec: Search tasks by title\n2\t\n3\t**Taiga:** #11\n4\t**Type:** Feature\n5\t**Branch:** feature/tp-11/search-tasks-by-title\n6\t\n7\t## Goal\n8\t\n9\tLet me type into a search box to narrow the visible task list down to tasks\n10\twhose title matches what I typed, so a long list stays usable.\n11\t\n12\t## Acceptance criteria\n13\t\n14\t1. **Given** tasks exist, **when** I type text into the search input,\n15\t   **then** only tasks whose title contains that text remain visible in the\n16\t   list.\n17\t2. **Given** I type text in a different case than the title (e.g. \"MEET\"\n18\t   against a task titled \"Team meeting\"), **when** filtering runs, **then**\n19\t   it still matches \u2014 matching is case-insensitive.\n20\t3. **Given** the search matches a substring anywhere in the title (not just\n21\t   the start), **when** filtering runs, **then** the task is shown \u2014 e.g.\n22\t   \"meet\" matches \"Team meeting\".\n23\t4. **Given** a state filter (Open/Done/All) is active and I also type a\n24\t   search term, **when** both are active, **then** the list shows only\n25\t   tasks that satisfy *both* \u2014 the same task-list array is narrowed by\n26\t   state first, then by title, exactly as `visibleTasks` already narrows by\n27\t   state in `frontend/src/App.jsx:29`. Search and state filter combine with\n28\t   AND, never override or reset each other.\n29\t5. **Given** my search term matches zero tasks under the current state\n30\t   filter, **when** the list would otherwise render, **then** an explicit\n31\t   message says nothing matched the search \u2014 distinct from the existing\n32\t   \"Nothing to do yet.\" / \"Nothing open right now.\" / \"Nothing done yet.\"\n33\t   copy in `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx:3-7`, which means \"this\n34\t   state filter is empty,\" not \"your search found nothing.\"\n35\t6. **Given** I clear the search input back to empty, **when** filtering\n36\t   runs, **then** all tasks reappear (subject only to the state filter).\n37\t7. **Given** the task list re-fetches after an add/complete/delete/edit\n38\t   (`refresh()` in `App.jsx:16`), **when** the refresh completes, **then**\n39\t   my typed search term is not cleared \u2014 it behaves like `filter`, which\n40\t   already survives refreshes because both live in `App` state, not in\n41\t   fetched data.\n42\t\n43\t## Non-goals\n44\t\n45\t- No backend involvement. The state filter has no server-side support today\n46\t  \u2014 `store.list()` (`backend/app/store.py:51`) always returns everything,\n47\t  and `App.jsx` narrows it client-side. Search follows the same pattern:\n48\t  no new query param, no new endpoint, no changes under `backend/`.\n49\t- No fuzzy or typo-tolerant matching. Literal case-insensitive substring\n50\t  only, per the request's own wording (\"case-insensitive... what is\n51\t  actually displayed\").\n52\t- No matching against fields other than the displayed title \u2014 not `id`,\n53\t  not `priority`.\n54\t- No highlighting of the matched substring inside the title.\n55\t- No debouncing/throttling the input. The store is in-memory with no\n56\t  pagination, and filtering is a synchronous array pass over data already\n57\t  in memory \u2014 the same cost the state-filter buttons already pay on every\n58\t  click.\n59\t- No persistence of the search term across a page reload. It is transient\n60\t  UI state, same lifecycle as `filter` (`App.jsx:14`), which also doesn't\n61\t  persist today.\n62\t- Does not change sort order \u2014 the existing high-priority-first sort\n63\t  (`App.jsx:35-37`) still applies to whatever the combined filters leave.\n64\t\n65\t## Affected areas\n66\t\n67\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 add a `search` state value alongside `filter`\n68\t  (line 14); extend the `visibleTasks` filter (lines 29-33) to also test\n69\t  the title; pass `search`/`setSearch` to the new search input and down to\n70\t  `TaskList`.\n71\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 `EMPTY_COPY` (lines 3-7) is\n72\t  keyed only by `filter`; needs a search-aware empty-state message per AC5.\n73\t- A new component under `frontend/src/components/` for the search input\n74\t  itself (placement/naming is a UX decision \u2014 it's a text input, not a\n75\t  toggle-button group, so it doesn't belong inside the existing\n76\t  `TaskFilter.jsx`, which renders `role=\"group\"` buttons).\n77\t- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styling for the new input, likely extending\n78\t  `.list-toolbar` (`App.css:33`) where `TaskFilter` and `ClearCompleted`\n79\t  already sit.\n80\t- No changes to `backend/` (see Non-goals).\n81\t\n82\t## Edge cases\n83\t\n84\t- **Empty store (no tasks at all):** falls through to the existing\n85\t  per-filter empty copy, not the new \"no search matches\" copy \u2014 there's\n86\t  nothing to have searched yet. Distinguish \"0 tasks total\" from \"0 tasks\n87\t  after search narrowed a non-empty list.\"\n88\t- **Search text with no tasks matching, under `filter=all` vs `open` vs\n89\t  `done`:** the \"no matches\" message applies in all three combinations\n90\t  (AC4 + AC5 together).\n91\t- **Whitespace-only search term:** should not throw or behave oddly;\n92\t  treating it as matching everything (empty-after-trim behaves like no\n93\t  search) is a reasonable default consistent with typical search-box UX.\n94\t- **Special characters in the search term** (e.g. `(`, `*`, `.`): must be\n95\t  treated as literal text to match, not a regex \u2014 a title containing\n96\t  literal `(` should be findable by typing `(`, and typing regex\n97\t  metacharacters must never throw.\n98\t- **Search term longer than any title, or containing characters no title\n99\t  has:** zero matches, same \"no matches\" message as AC5.\n100\t- **Clearing search while a state filter is still active:** returns to\n101\t  exactly the state-filtered list (AC6), not the unfiltered full list.\n102\t\n103\t## Open questions\n104\t\n105\tNone \u2014 the request is unambiguous enough to proceed on the defaults stated\n106\tabove (substring match, AND-combine with the state filter, transient\n107\tclient-side state). Exact placement and copy for the search input and the\n108\tnew empty-state message are UX decisions for the next stage, not product\n109\tdecisions requiring sign-off.\n110\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015Tmb7DeQirgpXfJudgArMY", "session_id": "04c2cf11-858c-4c93-a37f-ebb81b08252f"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:30:51Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 17, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Search tasks by title\n2\t\n3\t**Taiga:** #11\n4\t**Spec:** `docs/spec.md`\n5\t\n6\t## Conventions established\n7\t\n8\tRead `frontend/src/App.jsx`, `frontend/src/components/{TaskFilter,ClearCompleted,TaskCounts,AddTask,TaskList}.jsx`,\n9\tand `frontend/src/App.css` in full before deciding anything below.\n10\t\n11\t- No component library, no CSS-in-JS \u2014 plain function components, one per\n12\t  file, styled entirely through `App.css` class selectors.\n13\t- Text inputs (`AddTask.jsx:24-29`, `TaskList.jsx:77-84`) share one look:\n14\t  `border: 1px solid #ccd2d6; border-radius: 5px; font: inherit;` with\n15\t  `~0.55rem 0.7rem` padding, and get their accessible name from\n16\t  `aria-label` rather than a visible `<label>`.\n17\t- Muted/secondary text (`.empty`, `.loading`, `.task-counts`) uses\n18\t  `#6b7780` / `#5a646c` on the page's white card backgrounds.\n19\t- No component anywhere sets a custom `:focus` style \u2014 focus relies on the\n20\t  browser default outline throughout the app. Search follows the same\n21\t  default; introducing a custom ring here would make it the only styled\n22\t  focus state in the app, which is a bigger decision than this feature\n23\t  needs.\n24\t- `.list-toolbar` (`App.css:33-41`) is a `space-between` flex row holding\n25\t  exactly two visual groups today: `TaskFilter` on the left,\n26\t  `ClearCompleted` on the right.\n27\t\n28\t## Component: `frontend/src/components/SearchTasks.jsx` (new)\n29\t\n30\t```\n31\t<div className=\"search-tasks\">\n32\t  <input type=\"search\" aria-label=\"Search tasks by title\" placeholder=\"Search by title\" />\n33\t</div>\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t- Controlled input, `value`/`onChange` props from `App.jsx`, same shape as\n37\t  `TaskFilter`'s `value`/`onChange`.\n38\t- `type=\"search\"` (not `type=\"text\"`): in Chromium/Safari this renders a\n39\t  native \u00d7 clear button once there's text, which directly serves AC6\n40\t  (\"clear the search input\") without any extra markup. Firefox falls back\n41\t  to a plain text box with no native \u00d7; the input is still fully usable via\n42\t  keyboard/backspace there, so no polyfill is needed.\n43\t- `placeholder=\"Search by title\"` \u2014 matches `AddTask`'s placeholder voice\n44\t  (`\"What needs doing?\"`): short, no trailing ellipsis, since no existing\n45\t  placeholder in this codebase uses one.\n46\t- `aria-label=\"Search tasks by title\"` \u2014 same pattern as\n47\t  `aria-label=\"Filter tasks\"` on `TaskFilter`'s wrapping `div`.\n48\t\n49\t## Placement: `App.jsx`\n50\t\n51\tToday `.list-toolbar` has two flex children and relies on `space-between`\n52\tto push them to opposite edges. Adding `SearchTasks` as a third sibling\n53\twould make `space-between` spread all three apart evenly \u2014 search would\n54\tdrift away from the filter buttons it's meant to sit next to. Instead:\n55\t\n56\t```\n57\t<div className=\"list-toolbar\">\n58\t  <div className=\"toolbar-filters\">\n59\t    <SearchTasks value={search} onChange={setSearch} />\n60\t    <TaskFilter value={filter} onChange={setFilter} />\n61\t  </div>\n62\t  <ClearCompleted count={completedCount} onClear={...} />\n63\t</div>\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\tSearch sits **before** the state-filter buttons, left-most in the group:\n67\tit's the control most people reach for first on a long list, and the two\n68\tnarrowing controls (search, state) read left-to-right as one group,\n69\tvisually separated from the destructive/bulk `ClearCompleted` action on\n70\tthe far right. `toolbar-filters` keeps that pairing intact under\n71\t`space-between` and still wraps as a unit on narrow widths.\n72\t\n73\t`search` is new `App` state (`useState('')`) declared next to `filter`\n74\t(`App.jsx:14`) \u2014 same lifecycle: lives only in `App`, resets on reload,\n75\tsurvives `refresh()`.\n76\t\n77\t## Filtering behavior (`App.jsx`, extends lines 29-33)\n78\t\n79\tThe existing single-pass `visibleTasks` filter becomes two passes so the\n80\t\"state filter has nothing\" and \"search found nothing within the state\n81\tfilter\" cases can be told apart (needed for the empty-state copy below):\n82\t\n83\t1. `stateFiltered` \u2014 exactly today's `filter` logic (open/done/all),\n84\t   unchanged.\n85\t2. `visibleTasks` \u2014 `stateFiltered` narrowed by the trimmed,\n86\t   lower-cased search term as a plain substring test against the\n87\t   lower-cased title. An empty trimmed term matches everything (covers the\n88\t   whitespace-only edge case). No regex construction anywhere, so literal\n89\t   characters like `(` or `*` are matched as-is and can never throw.\n90\t\n91\tBoth passes read from the same `tasks` array already in state \u2014 no new\n92\tfetch, no debounce, matching the non-goals.\n93\t\n94\t`TaskList` needs one extra piece of information beyond today's `tasks` +\n95\t`filter`: whether the *state*-filtered set (before search) was non-empty.\n96\tPass `stateFiltered.length > 0` down as a boolean (e.g. `hasFilterResults`)\n97\talongside the current `search` string, so it can pick the right empty\n98\tmessage without recomputing anything.\n99\t\n100\t## Empty-state copy (`TaskList.jsx`, extends `EMPTY_COPY` at lines 3-7)\n101\t\n102\tPrecedence when the list to render is empty, in order:\n103\t\n104\t| Condition | Message shown | Existing/new |\n105\t|---|---|---|\n106\t| `tasks.length === 0` (store has nothing at all) | `EMPTY_COPY[filter]` (unchanged: \"Nothing to do yet.\" / \"Nothing open right now.\" / \"Nothing done yet.\") | existing |\n107\t| store has tasks, but `stateFiltered.length === 0` (this state filter has nothing, independent of search) | `EMPTY_COPY[filter]` | existing |\n108\t| `stateFiltered.length > 0` but search narrowed it to zero | new copy, see below | **new** |\n109\t\n110\tNew copy: `No tasks match \"{trimmed search term}\".` \u2014 e.g. typing `xyz`\n111\tagainst a list with no matching titles shows `No tasks match \"xyz\".`\n112\tStraight double quotes, plain punctuation, same terse voice as the\n113\texisting three strings; includes the actual term so the message is\n114\tlegible on its own if a screen reader announces it out of context.\n115\t\n116\tAccessibility addition: give the empty `<p className=\"empty\">` an\n117\t`aria-live=\"polite\"` (it doesn't have one today). Once search re-filters\n118\tthe list on every keystroke without a page navigation, a screen-reader\n119\tuser needs to be told the list just emptied out or repopulated \u2014 nothing\n120\ttoday announces that. This is a one-attribute addition to the existing\n121\telement, applied uniformly to all three existing empty messages and the\n122\tnew one, not a redesign of the component.\n123\t\n124\t## States\n125\t\n126\t**Populated, no search (unchanged behavior)**\n127\t```\n128\t[ Tasks ]\n129\t3 tasks open \u00b7 1 task done\n130\t[ What needs doing?          ] [Normal v] [Add]\n131\t[ \ud83d\udd0d Search by title    ] [All][Open][Done]         [Clear completed (1)]\n132\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n133\t\u2502 Team meeting            [Normal v] Edit Done Delete \u2502\n134\t\u2502 Buy milk                [High   v] Edit Done Delete \u2502\n135\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n136\t```\n137\t\n138\t**Populated, search narrows the list (AC1-3)**\n139\tTyping \"meet\" (any case) into search, filter = All:\n140\t```\n141\t[ \ud83d\udd0d meet\u2715              ] [All][Open][Done]         [Clear completed (1)]\n142\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n143\t\u2502 Team meeting            [Normal v] Edit Done Delete \u2502\n144\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n145\t```\n146\t\"Buy milk\" drops out immediately, no submit needed. The \u00d7 shown here is\n147\tthe native `type=\"search\"` clear control (Chromium/Safari only, see\n148\tabove).\n149\t\n150\t**Search + state filter combined, AND semantics (AC4)**\n151\tfilter = Done, search = \"meet\", and \"Team meeting\" is not done:\n152\t```\n153\t[ \ud83d\udd0d meet\u2715              ] [All][Open][Done*]        [Clear completed (0)]\n154\tNo tasks match \"meet\".\n155\t```\n156\t(`*` = active filter button.) The state filter isn't relaxed to show a\n157\tresult \u2014 both conditions apply together, per spec.\n158\t\n159\t**No matches (AC5)**\n160\tCovered by the case directly above \u2014 search is the only new empty state;\n161\tcopy is `No tasks match \"{term}\".` as specified.\n162\t\n163\t**Cleared search (AC6)**\n164\tDeleting the text (via backspace or the native \u00d7) returns synchronously to\n165\twhatever the current state filter shows \u2014 same render path as \"Populated,\n166\tno search\" above, just re-entered.\n167\t\n168\t**Search survives an add/complete/delete/edit refresh (AC7)**\n169\tNo visual state of its own \u2014 `search` lives in `App`, `refresh()` only\n170\ttouches `tasks`, so the input's typed value is untouched across a refresh.\n171\tWorth a callout only because it's easy to get wrong by accident (e.g. a\n172\tcareless reset alongside `filter`), not because it's visible.\n173\t\n174\t**Empty store, no tasks at all**\n175\tSearch box still renders (it's always-on in the toolbar, matching\n176\t`TaskFilter`/`ClearCompleted`'s current unconditional rendering), but the\n177\tmessage shown is the existing per-filter copy, never the new \"no search\n178\tmatches\" copy \u2014 there is nothing to have searched yet:\n179\t```\n180\t[ \ud83d\udd0d Search by title    ] [All][Open][Done]         [Clear completed (0)]\n181\tNothing to do yet.\n182\t```\n183\t\n184\t**Loading**\n185\tUnchanged: `TaskList` is replaced by `<p className=\"loading\">Loading\u2026</p>`,\n186\tbut the toolbar \u2014 including the new search box \u2014 still renders above it,\n187\texactly as `TaskFilter`/`ClearCompleted` already do during load. Typing\n188\tduring this brief window has no visible effect since `tasks` is still\n189\t`[]`; no special-cased disabled state is introduced, consistent with how\n190\tthe filter buttons behave today.\n191\t\n192\t**Interactive**\n193\t- *Empty/unfocused:* placeholder \"Search by title\" in the default muted\n194\t  placeholder color, `#ccd2d6` border.\n195\t- *Focused:* browser default focus outline (no custom ring \u2014 see\n196\t  conventions above).\n197\t- *Has text (Chromium/Safari):* native \u00d7 appears inside the input,\n198\t  clears on click, refocuses the input.\n199\t- *Has text (Firefox):* no native \u00d7; clearing is backspace/select-all,\n200\t  same as any other text input in this app.\n201\t\n202\t## Accessibility\n203\t\n204\t- Target size: input padding matches `.add-task input`\n205\t  (`0.55rem 0.7rem` vertical/horizontal) and `.filter-option`\n206\t  (`0.45rem 0.9rem`), so the search box sits at the same ~36-38px row\n207\t  height as the adjacent filter buttons \u2014 no separate sizing decision\n208\t  needed, it's already consistent with this toolbar row.\n209\t- Focus order: unchanged DOM-order tab sequence \u2014\n210\t  `AddTask` fields \u2192 `SearchTasks` input \u2192 `TaskFilter` buttons \u2192\n211\t  `ClearCompleted` \u2192 task rows. Matches the new left-to-right visual\n212\t  order in `toolbar-filters` above, so tab order and reading order agree.\n213\t- Accessible name: `aria-label=\"Search tasks by title\"` on the input\n214\t  itself (no visible `<label>`, consistent with `AddTask`'s title input\n215\t  and `TaskFilter`'s `aria-label=\"Filter tasks\"`).\n216\t- Live region: `aria-live=\"polite\"` added to the empty-state `<p>` (see\n217\t  above) so a screen-reader user is told when typing empties or\n218\t  repopulates the list.\n219\t- Contrast \u2014 no new color pairings are introduced; every color here is an\n220\t  existing token reused for its existing purpose:\n221\t  - Input text `#16191c` on white: contrast ratio **17.65:1** (computed:\n222\t    relative luminance of `#16191c` \u2248 0.00949, white = 1.0,\n223\t    (1.05)/(0.00949+0.05) = 17.65). Already the standing body-text color\n224\t    everywhere in the app.\n225\t  - Placeholder / new empty-state message text `#6b7780` on white:\n226\t    contrast ratio **4.59:1** (relative luminance \u2248 0.1789,\n227\t    (1.05)/(0.1789+0.05) = 4.59) \u2014 clears the 4.5:1 text minimum. Same\n228\t    token already used for `.empty`/`.loading` (`App.css:62`); this is\n229\t    its first use as a placeholder color specifically, so it's called out\n230\t    and verified rather than assumed to carry over.\n231\t  - Input border `#ccd2d6` on white card background: this is a\n232\t    non-text UI boundary (3:1 minimum applies, not 4.5:1) and is the same\n233\t    border token already used on every other input and the filter group\n234\t    in this app.\n235\t\n236\t## Styling (`App.css`)\n237\t\n238\tAdd, near `.list-toolbar` (`App.css:33-41`):\n239\t\n240\t```css\n241\t.toolbar-filters {\n242\t  display: flex;\n243\t  align-items: center;\n244\t  flex-wrap: wrap;\n245\t  gap: 0.6rem;\n246\t}\n247\t\n248\t.search-tasks input {\n249\t  min-width: 9rem;\n250\t  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;\n251\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n252\t  border-radius: 5px;\n253\t  font: inherit;\n254\t}\n255\t```\n256\t\n257\t`.list-toolbar { justify-content: space-between; ... }` (`App.css:33-40`)\n258\tis unchanged \u2014 it now spaces exactly two children again\n259\t(`.toolbar-filters` and `ClearCompleted`'s button), same as today.\n260\t`.list-toolbar .task-filter { margin-bottom: 0; }` (`App.css:41`) also\n261\tstays as-is; no change needed to `.task-filter` or `.filter-option`.\n262\t\n263\t## Traceability\n264\t\n265\t| Acceptance criterion | Design element |\n266\t|---|---|\n267\t| AC1 (typing narrows by title) | `SearchTasks` input + `visibleTasks` second filter pass |\n268\t| AC2 (case-insensitive) | Lower-cased comparison in the filter pass |\n269\t| AC3 (substring anywhere) | Plain `.includes()` substring test, no anchoring |\n270\t| AC4 (AND with state filter) | Two-pass filter: `stateFiltered` then search narrows further; \"search + state filter combined\" wireframe |\n271\t| AC5 (explicit no-match message) | New `No tasks match \"{term}\".` copy, precedence table |\n272\t| AC6 (clearing search restores state-filtered list) | \"Cleared search\" state; native \u00d7 on `type=\"search\"` |\n273\t| AC7 (search survives refresh) | `search` lives in `App` state alongside `filter`, untouched by `refresh()` |\n274\t| Edge: empty store | \"Empty store\" state \u2014 falls through to existing `EMPTY_COPY`, never the new copy |\n275\t| Edge: whitespace-only search | Trimmed-term-empty-matches-all rule in the filtering section |\n276\t| Edge: special/regex characters | Plain substring test, never constructs a `RegExp` |\n277\t| Edge: search + each of Open/Done/All | Precedence table's three rows cover state-empty vs. search-empty independently for any `filter` value |\n278\t\n279\t## Non-goals confirmed unaffected\n280\t\n281\tNo highlighting of matched substrings, no debounce, no backend changes,\n282\tno persistence across reload, no change to sort order \u2014 none of the\n283\tstates or styling above touch any of these; consistent with `docs/spec.md`.\n284\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DzfgxZLyrHu7MVAFF4SMFa", "session_id": "04c2cf11-858c-4c93-a37f-ebb81b08252f"}}
